	"observations": [
		"Independent Node processes elect one owner. SIGKILL preserves a pending slot; a successor fences stale SQL, checkpoint and release operations.",
		"Expired ownership rolls back a transaction; a lost checkpoint COMMIT acknowledgement resumes from database progress without replaying the mutation.",
		"Locked retention rows, active source publishers and deferred object deletions keep the run partial instead of reporting zero-work success.",
		"Negative sweeps paginate and preserve positive/reversal provenance and removal tombstones. Malformed opinion provenance fails without replacing evidence.",
		"Regression tests exposed and repaired false completion with 205 orphan marks and repeated restart of slow protected pages; name plus exact generation now resumes within a page.",
		"Node shutdown and error tests cover cancellation during startup/work, late completion, fatal exceptions and a hung close; provider and credential sentinels are absent from process output.",
		"The packaged job uses actual Neon adapter TLS and GCS JSON API transport against local fixtures. SIGKILL after HTTP deletion leaves its durable mark; a new container recovers the absent object and completes the original slot. A further duplicate is idle.",
		"All eight final-image container cases pass, including retained public/operator and TLS lifecycle cases. No container OOM was observed."
	],
	"verification_sequence": "Initial repository checks stopped on formatting and a template-literal lint rule; both were corrected. Final repository checks passed. The lint-clean image was rebuilt, then all 95 PostgreSQL and eight container tests passed. Documentation and the local qualification record were added afterward; workflow YAML was parsed separately. No runtime source changed after these final checks.",
